# Party banter while exploring Death House (and the road into it). Each node is one short exchange; its opening
# `if` is the gate. The game plays an eligible node (gate true) at a quiet moment, once each.
# Pregen voices: docs/voice/{ilse_varga, tamsin_tealeaf, hedda_ironvow, silvain_aster}.md. Class, species and
# background lines are written so any such character could say them.

~ bt_too_clean
if name:ilse_varga and name:tamsin_tealeaf and visited:dh_main_hall and not flag.death_house_completed
  interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Somebody dusts this place.
  interject name:ilse_varga: Nobody's lived here in years.
  interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: That's what I said. Somebody dusts this place.
endif
-> END

~ bt_wolves_on_the_road
if flag.mists_wolves_cowed and visited:death_house_ground and class:fighter and class:cleric
  interject class:fighter: Those wolves gave way like a picket line. Someone's expecting us.
  interject class:cleric: Then let's be late. Rudely, unforgivably late.
endif
-> END

~ bt_wolf_blood
if flag.mists_wolves_fought and visited:dh_den and name:hedda_ironvow and name:silvain_aster
  interject name:hedda_ironvow: Eleven wolf heads on that wall, and wolves waiting for us on the road. I don't think that's a coincidence.
  interject name:silvain_aster: It's a grudge. The house hunted someone's wolves, and now someone's wolves hunt the house's guests.
endif
-> END

~ bt_locked_from_outside
if visited:dh_childrens_room and name:tamsin_tealeaf and name:ilse_varga
  interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: I don't like rooms that lock from the outside. I've been in a few.
  interject name:ilse_varga: You got out.
  interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: I always get out. That's not the same as liking it.
endif
-> END

~ bt_nursery_locks
if visited:dh_childrens_room and class:rogue and not name:tamsin_tealeaf
  interject class:rogue: Locks on the outside of a children's door. Whoever fitted those knew exactly what they were for.
endif
-> END

~ bt_theology_of_debt
if flag.death_house_read_strahd_letter and name:hedda_ironvow and name:silvain_aster
  interject name:silvain_aster: His letter treats worship as a bad debt.
  interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. Most gods would agree. They just send kinder letters.
  interject name:silvain_aster: Do they? I've never had one.
  interject name:hedda_ironvow: You've never asked.
endif
-> END

~ bt_the_signature
if flag.death_house_read_strahd_letter and name:ilse_varga and name:tamsin_tealeaf
  interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Maybe it's just his initial, Ilse. Lots of people start with S.
  interject name:ilse_varga: It's a signature, Tealeaf. It's a promise.
endif
-> END

~ bt_windmill
if flag.death_house_found_deeds and name:tamsin_tealeaf and name:silvain_aster
  interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: So when this is over, we retire to the windmill.
  interject name:silvain_aster: There is a noise under this house that suggests "over" is optimistic.
  interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Windmill, Silvain. Hold on to the windmill.
endif
-> END

~ bt_dwarf_stonework
if visited:dh_family_crypts and species:dwarf
  interject species:dwarf: Good stonework, all of it. Somebody with a real chisel cut these crypts. Pity about the tenants.
endif
-> END

~ bt_elf_portraits
if visited:dh_upper_hall and species:elf
  interject species:elf: I remember the fashions in the oldest of these portraits. They were embarrassing then, too.
endif
-> END

~ bt_halfling_dumbwaiter
if visited:dh_kitchen and species:halfling and class:fighter
  interject species:halfling: I'd fit in that dumbwaiter, you know.
  interject class:fighter: You are not getting in the dumbwaiter.
  interject species:halfling: I said I'd fit. I didn't say I'd go. ...I might go.
endif
-> END

~ bt_soldier_barracks
if visited:dh_cult_dormitory and background:soldier
  interject background:soldier: Bunks in rows, kit on pegs, a roster on the wall. They ran it like a barracks. That's how you get ordinary people to do this.
endif
-> END

~ bt_criminal_keepsakes
if visited:dh_reliquary and background:criminal
  interject background:criminal: Shelves of other people's lockets. The cult robbed its dead and kept a tidy shop. I'm not taking any of those. Not those.
endif
-> END

~ bt_children_truth
if flag.death_house_children_truth and name:hedda_ironvow and name:ilse_varga
  interject name:hedda_ironvow: They starved, waiting for a door to open.
  interject name:ilse_varga: Then we open every door in this house.
  interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. Most of them will be worse.
  interject name:ilse_varga: Every door.
endif
-> END

~ bt_humming
if flag.death_house_children_riding and not flag.death_house_children_at_rest
  Narrator: One of you is humming a nursery tune that none of you know.
  Player: Who's humming?
  Narrator: Nobody answers, and the humming stops. Then, very quietly, someone giggles.
endif
-> END

~ bt_lure
if flag.death_house_saw_through_lure and class:cleric and class:wizard
  interject class:cleric: The children in the road were bait. The house dangles them and waits.
  interject class:wizard: An old trick. Effective, apparently. We're inside.
endif
-> END

~ bt_escape_candlestick
if flag.death_house_refused and not flag.death_house_completed and name:ilse_varga and name:tamsin_tealeaf
  interject name:ilse_varga: Keep moving. Don't touch anything.
  interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: I wasn't going to touch anything.
  interject name:ilse_varga: You're holding a candlestick.
  interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: It touched me first.
endif
-> END

~ bt_lorghoth_slain
if flag.death_house_lorghoth_slain and class:fighter and class:wizard
  interject class:fighter: We killed the thing in the basement.
  interject class:wizard: We killed a thing in the basement. I'd hesitate to call it the thing.
endif
-> END

~ bt_after_the_altar
if flag.death_house_sacrificed
  Narrator: Nobody counts off anymore. Nobody needs to be told the number.
endif
-> END
